="lazy"> <span class="video-play"><svg width="32" height="32" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><polygon points="6 4 20 12 6 20 6 4"></polygon></svg></span> </button> </div> </div> </section>  <section id="about" style="background: var(--white)"> <div class="container"> <div class="about-grid"> <div class="about-copy"> <div class="section-head" style="margin-bottom: 20px"> <h2>Why owners hire us.</h2> </div> <h3>Marketing built around the work, not the retainer.</h3> <p>22 Local Marketing was built because the agency industry kept selling the same recycled retainer to tree and land owners who deserved better. Generic templates, vanity dashboards, monthly invoices, no accountability for revenue.</p> <p>Three things tend to matter most to the owners who stay. You get a fast answer, and it comes from Connor, not a ticket queue. We treat your numbers as our problem rather than handing over a list of completed tasks. And there is a method behind the work, one that produces results when it gets followed. That last part is a real condition, not a figure of speech. When a client skips the photos, sits on review requests, or holds back ad budget, the method slows down, and we will say so rather than quietly absorb it.</p> <p>One team runs SEO, paid, web, and reporting in house, so nothing gets handed off and lost. Reporting is tied to calls and booked jobs, not impressions.</p> <div class="about-bullets"> <div class="about-bullet"><div class="about-bullet-tick"><svg width="10" height="10" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3.5"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"></polyline></svg></div><div>Connor answers personally. Not a ticket queue.</div></div> <div class="about-bullet"><div class="about-bullet-tick"><svg width="10" height="10" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3.5"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"></polyline></svg></div><div>One team, in house. SEO, paid, web, and reporting.</div></div> <div class="about-bullet"><div class="about-bullet-tick"><svg width="10" height="10" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3.5"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"></polyline></svg></div><div>Reported against calls and booked jobs, not impressions.</div></div> <div class="about-bullet"><div class="about-bullet-tick"><svg width="10" height="10" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3.5"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"></polyline></svg></div><div>No long contracts. Month to month, always.</div></div> <div class="about-bullet"><div class="about-bullet-tick"><svg width="10" height="10" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3.5"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"></polyline></svg></div><div>You own everything we build. Site, GBP, accounts.</div></div> <div class="about-bullet"><div class="about-bullet-tick"><svg width="10" height="10" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3.5"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"></polyline></svg></div><div>Real photos, real copy, no templates.</div></div> </div> <a href="#contact" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" data-quote>Book a strategy call <span class="btn-arrow">→</span></a> </div> <div class="about-card"> <div class="about-card-eyebrow">→ Founder</div> <div class="about-photo"><img src="/founder.png" alt="Connor Dann, founder of 22 Local Marketing" loading="lazy"></div> <div class="about-name">Connor Dann</div> <div class="about-role">Founder · 22 Local Marketing</div> <div class="about-quote">"Most agencies sell hours. We sell outcomes. The difference shows up in the work, and you'll feel it in the first 30 days."</div> </div> </div> </div> </section>  <section id="faq"> <div class="container"> <div class="section-head"> <h2>Questions worth answering up front.</h2> </div> <div class="faq-list"> <div class="faq-item open"><button class="faq-q">I've tried a marketing agency before and it didn't work. Why would this be different?</button><div class="faq-a">That's the objection we hear most, and it's usually earned. Here's what we can point at instead of arguing. Our clients average 60-plus phone calls and 40-plus form leads a month at under $50 per lead. One land management client in Northwest Ohio went from no search presence at all to ranking for over 1,000 queries, with 160-plus of them in Google's top three, inside six months. Our own profile sits at 5.0 stars across 36 verified Google reviews.<br><br>Now the honest part. Expect 3 to 5 leads in the first couple of months, then building from there. Not fifty. If someone promises you fifty in month one, that's the version of this that didn't work last time. You're month to month the whole way, so if we're not earning it you leave.</div></div> <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q">How long until I see results?</button><div class="faq-a">Expect 3 to 5 leads in the first couple of months, and growth from there. Paid usually moves first because you're buying placement. Map pack movement tends to show up inside 30 to 60 days. Organic ranking shifts take 3 to 6 months depending on where you're starting. We'll give you our read on your specific market on the first call rather than a generic number.</div></div> <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q">Do I have to sign a long contract?</button><div class="faq-a">No. Every engagement is month-to-month. If you want to stop, you stop. We earn the renewal by performing, not by trapping you.</div></div> <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q">Do I own the website and accounts you build?</button><div class="faq-a">Yes. You own the website, the domain, the GBP, the ad accounts, the call tracking, and everything in between. If we ever part ways, you walk with everything.</div></div> <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q">What does it actually cost?</button><div class="faq-a">Engagements are scoped to the work and your market. Most full-service clients land in the range you'd expect for an in-house marketing hire, but with a whole team behind it. We give you a flat number on the second call once we understand the scope.</div></div> <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q">Will you work with my existing website?</button><div class="faq-a">Sometimes yes. If the bones are good, we tune it. If it's holding you back, we rebuild it. The audit tells us which one. Most clients end up with a rebuild because the gap to top-of-industry is bigger than it looks from the inside.</div></div> <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q">Do you only work with tree and land companies?</button><div class="faq-a">That's where we focus, and it's where most of our clients are. The playbook came out of tree care and land management, so we know the search terms, the seasonality, and the way these jobs get bought.<br><br>We do take on other home service contractors when the fit is right. Electrical, plumbing, HVAC, roofing, landscaping, grading, and similar trades all run on the same method, since the lead is a phone call and the job happens at a property. Ask on the first call and we'll tell you whether we're the right fit.</div></div> </div> </div> </section>  <section id="contact"> <div class="container"> <div class="cta-block"> <div> <div class="cta-eyebrow">→ Free 30-minute call</div> <h2>Let's see if the numbers work.</h2> <p>One call, no pitch deck. We look at your business, your market, and tell you straight whether we can move the needle. If not, we point you at someone who can.</p> <div class="cta-points"> <div class="cta-point"><div class="cta-point-num">→</div><div><div class="cta-point-title">No pitch deck</div><div class="cta-point-desc">We come ready to talk about your business, not ours.</div></div></div> <div class="cta-point"><div class="cta-point-num">→</div><div><div class="cta-point-title">Honest answer</div><div class="cta-point-desc">If we can't help, we say so on the call.</div></div></div> <div class="cta-point"><div class="cta-point-num">→</div><d